          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theories"} dependent type theories
            with more than one layer of type, function extension types are types which behave like
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+types"} function types
            except the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain"} domain
            is the outer layer (or equivalent) of type rather than the normal layer of type.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#in_dependent_type_theory_with_second_layer_for_propositions  In dependent type theory with second layer for propositions
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            with a second layer of propositions
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} prop
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \; \mathrm{prop}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inference+rules"} inference rules
            for extension types are given as follows:
          %p Formation rules for extension types:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
